<Docs title="Bookmarks" description="Pin frequently used directories in grüt for instant one-key access.">
  <h1>Bookmarks</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Bookmarks let you pin directories for quick navigation. Jump to any
    bookmarked path with a single keystroke instead of traversing the file
    tree.
  </p>

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    The bookmark manager stores a list of directory paths that you access
    frequently. Bookmarks are persisted to a TOML file alongside your
    configuration, so they survive restarts. You can seed initial bookmarks
    in your config file and add or remove them interactively at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Adding &amp; Removing Bookmarks</h2>
  <p>
    Navigate to any directory in the file tree and press the bookmark key
    to add it. Open the bookmark overlay to see all saved bookmarks,
    select one to jump to it, or delete bookmarks you no longer need.
  </p>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: 'B', action: 'Open bookmarks overlay' },
    { key: 'Enter', action: 'Jump to selected bookmark' },
    { key: 'd', action: 'Delete selected bookmark' },
    { key: 'r', action: 'Rename selected bookmark' },
    { key: 'Esc', action: 'Close bookmarks overlay' },
  ]} />

  <h2>Persistence</h2>
  <p>
    Bookmarks are stored in a separate TOML file in your grüt config
    directory. The bookmark manager loads saved bookmarks on startup and
    merges them with any paths defined in your configuration. Changes are
    written to disk immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>Configuration Reference</h2>
  <pre><code>[bookmarks]
paths = [             # Seed bookmarks from config
  "~/projects",
  "~/dotfiles",
]
show_in_sidebar = true # Show bookmarks section in sidebar</code></pre>

  <h2>Related</h2>
